<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bopolu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bopolu is a town in north-western Liberia, now the capital of Gbarpolu County. In the early 19th century it was the centre of the Condo Confederation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-boso">Sao Boso</a>, a market town where caravans from the interior exchanged goods with traders from the coast. Agents of the American settlers at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monrovia">Monrovia</a> visited it to secure trade routes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bopolu.jpg" alt="Bopolu" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S. Army Corps of Engineers Europe District from Wiesbaden, Germany · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:By_chance,_FEST_engineer_%E2%80%98comes_across%E2%80%99_cousin_in_Liberia_(15766600347).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
